# Poetry
#   Similar to Pipfile.lock, it's generally recommended to not commit poetry.lock
#   to version control. This is especially true for libraries not intended for
#   public consumption (i.e. internal-use libraries). However, there are cases
#   where committing poetry.lock makes sense, specifically when versioning
#   library applications to guarantee that all developers/clients/contractors
#   are using the exact same dependencies.
#   https://python-poetry.org/docs/basic-usage/#committing-your-poetry-lock-file-to-version-control
poetry.lock

.lsp/
.clj-kondo/